I can offer nothing better than a "me, too" - i think it'll be a good
idea to max out dagger skill for a powerful ranged attack; and _if_
you use a dagger as secondary, maxing out twoweapon combat may give an
effect, too (iirc, raising twoweapon to "expert" will only give you a
profit if you're actually using weapons you're also "expert" in).
Using the silver dagger as secondary is an o.k. choice - a little bit
less damage than a sabre, but lighter and less skillpoint-spreading
required.

> I've ascended 2 rogues this year and I believe both ascended
> using Stormbringer. The level draining wasn't particularly
> helpful in a fight to the death since the HP go down faster
> than the max HP.

It does a bit more: the level-draining weakens a monster - it is less
likely to hit and it will become less likely to cast its most powerful
spell (monster casting takes monster level into account). Rodney is
also easier to kill when you level-drain him, because his maxhp going
down mean that his "runaway threshold" (the number of hitpoints he'll
start to zap to the staircase and regenerate, which seems to be
defined as a fraction of his maxhitpoints) also sinks, to the point
where he'll be bold enough to stay in the fight while being low enough
on hits that he can be killed in one round.
And whenever you drain a level, this will heal you a little bit; if
you're well-armoured, this can completely offset the hurt incurred by
a whole pack of monsters wailing on you.

